.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-RENAME" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-rename - Rename a durable tunnel


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel rename <tunnel> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a durable tunnel selected by its exact ID or current name. The command reads the current resource version before changing its name and reports the server's canonical result. Existing routes, connectors and access policy remain attached to the same tunnel. Refresh and retry if another writer changed it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rename

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
